# How to cite this corpus. This is distinct from citing ComStock itself: cite a document's
# publication URL (line 1 of every processed file) for ComStock's content, and this record
# for the corpus as an artifact. See AGENTS.md "Citing".
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, cite it as below and name the release tag you read, so the
  citation resolves to the same bytes later. Cite ComStock's own documents by their
  publication URL.
type: dataset
title: "buildstock-corpus: AI-ready ComStock documentation corpus"
abstract: >-
  ComStock's documentation -- the technical reference, the ComStock site's pages, and the
  upgrade-measure reports -- extracted to clean, release-tagged markdown with a provenance
  manifest, hand-authored transcriptions of tables and figures the extractors cannot
  recover, a human-readable map, and a machine index. One dataset release per folder.
authors:
  - family-names: Klun
    given-names: Lauren
    affiliation: National Laboratory of the Rockies
repository-code: https://github.com/NatLabRockies/buildstock-corpus
url: https://github.com/NatLabRockies/buildstock-corpus
license: BSD-3-Clause
# The release tag; replace with the one you read if it is later. No DOI is minted for this
# corpus.
version: comstock_amy2018_2025_release_3-v1
date-released: 2026-10-08
keywords:
  - ComStock
  - BuildStock
  - building stock
  - documentation corpus
  - retrieval-augmented generation
references:
  - type: report
    title: ComStock Reference Documentation
    authors:
      - family-names: Parker
        given-names: Andrew
      - name: et al.
    institution:
      name: National Renewable Energy Laboratory
    year: 2023
    number: NREL/TP-5500-83819
    url: https://www.nlr.gov/docs/fy23osti/83819.pdf
    notes: >-
      The published ComStock reference; the corpus's technical_reference source is its
      per-release LaTeX. Attribute ComStock data per
      https://natlabrockies.github.io/ComStock.github.io/docs/citation.html.
